  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "9.6.0.11-beta\nFixed flex layout percentage-width items being re-resolved against the page width (instead of the flex container) when a child block opened its layout options. Explicit percentage or absolute widths are now correctly pinned to the flex algorithm's container-relative resolved value. Grow-only items (no explicit width) continue to use fill-width behaviour so their padding/border stays within column bounds.\nFixed flex wrap row-breaking with percentage item widths: GetItemMinWidth previously returned the raw number from a Unit (e.g. 45 for 45%) instead of resolving it against the container, causing all items to appear to fit in one row regardless of their actual pt widths.\nAdded Flex_61, Flex_62, Flex_63, Flex_64 layout unit tests covering: flex-grow distribution, explicit fixed widths with no grow, percentage widths resolved against the flex container, and 3-row wrap layout with 45%+100%+45% items.\n\n9.6.0.10-beta\nPre-load header/footer template components during the DataBind phase so that remote image requests in headers and footers are registered before Layout runs. In WASM (and other async-only environments) there is no synchronous HTTP fallback, so images whose requests are only registered at Layout time are never fulfilled. Fixed HasAdornments to check the template properties directly instead of the post-bind list (which was always empty, preventing the fix from running). Removed the now-unnecessary LayoutEngineHTMLBody override.\n\n9.6.0.9-beta\nFixed flex layout bug where min-height on a flex item caused its width to be inflated by the item's left margin (double-margin application in EnsureContentsFit when SetContentSize was called after Close).\nFixed flex-grow, flex-shrink and flex-basis set via CSS class rules (not inline style) being ignored in ComputeColumnWidths — now uses the full computed style via GetAppliedStyle + StyleStack + BuildFullStyle so CSS class-driven flex sizing works correctly.\n\n9.6.0.8-beta\nAdded support for the CSS aspect-ratio property (e.g. aspect-ratio: 16/9), including deriving it from an <img> element's width/height attributes as a natural-size hint. When CSS explicitly sets only one of width/height, the other dimension is now derived from the aspect-ratio (explicit CSS or intrinsic attributes) instead of being forced to a literal pixel size that could fight the styled dimension and distort the image. Applies to both raster and SVG image sizing.\n\n9.6.0.7-beta\nBREAKING CHANGE: <img width> / <img height> attributes now match the HTML5 spec - they set the image's intrinsic pixel size (a plain non-negative integer) instead of accepting arbitrary CSS units directly. A bare width=\"50%\" or width=\"40pt\" attribute on <img> will now throw a parse exception; move percentage or point-based sizing into style=\"width:...; height:...\" instead. Also added a style attribute mapping to <colgroup>/<col>.\n\n9.6.0.6-beta\nFixed LayoutEngineFlexGrid column widths for spanned cells - a cell spanning multiple grid columns now sums the widths of all the tracks it spans, instead of only receiving a single track's width.\n\n9.6.0.5-beta\nAdded full support for HTML table colgroup/col elements - column width, background, alignment and class styles now apply per-column to matching cells in the table layout engine, without overwriting a cell's own explicit style. Fixed the col/colgroup span calculation (a span of N now covers exactly N columns). Added CSS grid-column/grid-row parsing and span support, flexbox align-self and order properties, the flex-shrink algorithm for overflowing flex rows, and the CSS anonymous box algorithm for display:table/table-row/table-cell content that isn't explicitly wrapped. Fixed legacy <font size> handling for values pasted from Apple Pages.\n\n9.6.0.4-beta\nFixed an infinite pagination/stack overflow bug where a page-break request (e.g. break-after: always) originating from within a page header or footer's own content would repeatedly regenerate new pages without end. Header/footer content can no longer trigger page breaks.\n\n9.6.0.3-beta\nRolled back Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration/Logging dependencies to 8.x - the 10.x versions introduced in 9.6.0.2-beta pulled in a .NET 10 requirement that broke WASM compatibility.\n\n9.6.0.2-beta\nAdded support for asynchronous document and component parsing\n\n9.6.0.1-beta\nNEW: Added support for display flex layout.\nNEW: Added support for display grid layout\nNEW: Added support for table-x layout\nNEW: Added support for z-index rendering\nNEW: Added support for column balancing\n\nAdded jQuery-esque FindMatches with CSS selectors and support chained queries.\nAdded updates to support to preserve meta-* and data-* attributes (PR #173 Damir Liask)\nAdded fallback to model and values if property is not found (PR #173 Damir Liask)\nImproved data-url resiliance for parsing and case in-sensitivity (PR #173 Damir Liask)\nImproved config options changing to a list rather than array and allowing coded updates\n\nFixed an issue with with multiple returns\nFixed issue with CSS var default values being treated as properties\nFixed issue with display grid layout for and cascading CSS\nFixed issue with floats after balanced columns\n        \n        \n        \n9.5.0.1\nBREAKING RELEASE\nRemoved support for Net Standard 2.0, and Image Sharp updated to 3.1.2\nAll libraries updated to include dotnet 8/9/10\nAdded support image format webP \nImproved support for referenced SVG img\nClean up codebase to remove compiler warnings\n\n9.3.1.0\nFixes for break-before/after to take proiority over page-break-before\nFixes for @page to support margins, along with :first, :left and :right pseudo classes\n\n9.3.0.0\nCSS updates for rowspan on table cells, column-rules, contain on background images, border-radius on individual corners and CSS variables can now be modified in document properties.\nFixed page sizing in groups with fallback on following pages, whitespace hadling in soft returns, and SVG img placement and sizing.\nAdded *initial* implementation for flex-box, flex-grid, and table-xxx display\nConfiguration improvements incuding cusom image factories and custom expression functions.\n        \n9.2.0.3\nFixed styling issue when components are hidden using css.\n\n9.2.0.2\nFixed repeating raster background images with cover size\n\n9.2.0.1\nAdded support for repeating SVG background images from Data urls\n        \n9.2.0.0\nPublic release will all added features from the betas. Too many to list, but consult the documentation here https://www.paperworkday.info/learning/ and the refererence section here https://www.paperworkday.info/reference/\n        \n9.1.2-rc.5/6\nCouple of fixes for overflowing tables in a kept together parent, and svg font-weight bold and light are now supported and fixed an issue with the reverse function.\n        \n9.1.2-rc.4\nWorking modification of PDFs and templates using framesets and frames and support for SVG background images with opacity. \n\n9.1.0.7-beta\nFirst release of framesets for trimming and merging documents. Also hiding variables that do not have any content.\n\n9.0.0.1-rc.3\nAdded extra html entity values to match available sources.\n\n9.0.0.1-rc.2\nFixes for template parsing and added data-content to the template element, plus minor fixes and unit test updates. Second release candidate.\n\n9.0.0.1-rc.1\nMinor fixes for layout. First release candidate.\n        \n9.0.0.1-beta\nFixed a minor layout issue with multiple footer elementnamed components being applite to a page footer, and also header.\n        \n9.0.0.0-beta\nCompletely updated version for .NET 9.0 with support for html, css, svg and binding in a WASM compatible package with remote asset and content requests.\nNOTE: If upgrading, PLEASE CHECK THE OUTPUT of your documents before releasing.\n\nSee: https://paperwork.help/changelog/scryber_core.html for a full break down.",
